# Local configuration. Every one of these can hold the signing secret, so the
# patterns are wildcards rather than exact names: wrangler loads `.env`,
# `.env.local`, `.env.<environment>` and `.env.<environment>.local`, and the
# smoke test parks a `.dev.vars.smoke-stash.<pid>` for the length of its run.
#
# The committed template is `.vars.template` — not `.dev.vars.example`, which
# nothing here creates. It matches none of these patterns and is tracked.
.env*
.dev.vars*
!.env.example

.claude/
.agents/
skills-lock.json

ralph-logs/

handoff/

scripts/ralph.config.sh
